The premise behind the last two woodpecker.yml commits was FALSE, and
the falsifier is the direct observation the item asked for: the owner's
Woodpecker transcript of the INV-titih PR pipeline (#1136) shows every
step executing — lint, whole-tree strict mypy, audit, dco (its original
`event`+`path` AND form working, CI_COMMIT_TARGET_BRANCH resolved),
verify-generated, build-grammars, the v2 self-claims-gate's first live
run PASSING ("18 claims unchanged"), and pytest (9,240 tests, changed
files at 100%). Path conditions evaluate correctly on PR events.

Where the false premise came from: auto-pr's poll telemetry prints a
"[Ns]" line only on STATE TRANSITIONS and a dot per 10-second tick in
between. I read "[10s] waiting … ✅ CI Passed" as an 11-second pass, on
every log I checked. Counting the dots those logs actually contain:
zuhig ~4 min, titih ~11 min (matching #1136's contents), others
~1.5 min. Both "failed predictions" that escalated the theory (the fix
PR and the probe PR still "fast") were the same artifact, re-read twice.

This commit reverts the two changes shipped under the false premise:
- the twelve-step event-split (restored to the original path-scoped
  `when` forms, which were correct);
- the "config is evaluated from the target branch" header note
  (unverified, and now unnecessary as an explanation).

It keeps, corrected: the retirement of the genuinely stale "VERIFY the
exact context at cutover" header note, replaced by a note that teaches
the next reader how to read the poll telemetry (count the dots), and a
CHANGELOG retraction entry replacing the false one. INV-tisug is
resolved 'satisfied' — the invariant it states holds and always held —
with the full retraction recorded on the item.

Net positive by-product of the episode: the self-claims-gate's per-PR
arm is now LIVE-VERIFIED (noted on WI-ninoz).

